# Docker Hub (not in CI)

GitHub Actions **does not** build or push the server Docker image. CI and release workflows only test, lint, and publish GitHub Release binaries.

## What CI does

| Push type | GitHub CI | Docker Hub (`dendlomm/gsbs-server`) |
|-----------|-----------|-------------------------------------|
| `git push origin main` | test, lint, build binaries | **No** |
| `git push origin vX.Y.Z` | release workflow → GitHub Release | **No** |

## When the user wants Docker Hub updated

After a release tag (or anytime):

1. Build and push locally — see [docs/DOCKER.md](docs/DOCKER.md) (Pushing to Docker Hub), or
2. Run `./script/release.sh [VERSION]` if using the full local release path (includes optional Docker push).

Never commit Docker Hub credentials; use `docker login` locally only.

## When the user says "push to GitHub" (ambiguous)

- **Code sync only** → push branch (`main` or feature branch).
- **Deploy / release / publish client+server binaries** → tag push per [push-releases.mdc](push-releases.mdc).
- **Also update Docker Hub** → local docker build/push after release; CI will not do it.
